# Live runtime state: conversation/cache databases, request blobs, model logs.
# A process started from the repository root with a relative store path leaves these four
# beside .gitignore. They are the same runtime state as data/runtime/, in the wrong
# place, and the first sweep of this batch found 19 MB of them untracked and committable.
/blobs/
/cache/
/events/
/locks/
# This is personal session state and retrieval cache, not curated evidence.
# Curated fixtures, review batches and saved source pages stay tracked under
# data/processed, data/registry, research/ and tmp/pdfs.
data/runtime/
tmp/chrome-profile/
# Throwaway directories the test suite creates under tmp/ (mkdtemp debris).
tmp/tmp*/
# Runtime chat stores and the screenshot serving copy: session state, not curated evidence.
tmp/*.sqlite
tmp/screenshots/
tmp/npm-cache/
# The React build output and its dependencies: reproducible from frontend/ with npm ci && npm run build.
web/dist/
frontend/node_modules/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Local editor/assistant caches.
.serena/

# Local project dependency environment.
.venv/

# Local QA harness debris: the driver's own directory, headless-browser profiles, driver logs and the
# per-process session token this machine writes while a workspace is being tested. None of it is curated
# evidence, and the saved source pages under tmp/pdfs stay tracked.
nohup.out
tmp/*.log
tmp/qa/
tmp/qa-browser/
tmp/qa-chrome-profile*/
tmp/qa-home/
tmp/qa-session.txt
tmp/qa-token.txt
# Any session token this machine writes while testing, whatever name it is given: the token is per process
# and must never be committed. Measured 18 September 2026: a second token file (tmp/qa-acceptance-token.txt)
# slipped past the two exact names above and reached the index.
tmp/*token*

# Playwright run artifacts. The reviewed baselines under tests/ui/*-snapshots stay tracked; these do not.
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/blob-report/
frontend/.playwright/
tmp/npm-cache/
# The vision toolkit's own scratch (crops, heatmaps, reports) and a font probe's installed modules: both are
# machine-local tooling output, not evidence, and 2 MB of node_modules under research/ is neither.
.dsh-vision-toolkit/
research/design/probe-fonts/

# The scheduled refresh's own runtime state: a log, a lock and the last run's outcome. Machine-local.
data/runtime/refresh/

# Scratch scripts from working sessions. Never part of the product, and one of them had a real API key
# in it on a public remote. Keep them on disk; keep them out of the repository.
tmp/
